", "/^\\s*0?7\\s*[:.]\\s*05\\s*(a\\.?m\\.?|p\\.?m\\.?)?\\s*$/i"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "adv": [{"id": "m3u08s1a01", "type": "short", "prompt": "* Advanced. A film starts at 5:40 and lasts 45 minutes. Ends? Write it like 4:05.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["6:25", "/^\\s*0?6\\s*[:.]\\s*25\\s*(a\\.?m\\.?|p\\.?m\\.?)?\\s*$/i"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u08s1a02", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. At 3:30, why is the hour hand between 3 and 4, not on 3?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "half way / moves", "kw": ["half|between|move|30"]}], "need": 1, "model": "The hour hand moves slowly; half an hour past 3 it is halfway to 4.", "hint": "", "reason": "The hour hand moves slowly; half an hour past 3 it is halfway to 4."}, {"id": "m3u08s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. How many times does the minute hand go round in 3 hours?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "more": [{"id": "m3u08s1m01", "type": "short", "prompt": "Half past 2? Write it like 4:05.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["2:30", "/^\\s*0?2\\s*[:.]\\s*30\\s*(a\\.?m\\.?|p\\.?m\\.?)?\\s*$/i"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u08s1m02", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quarter past 9? Write it like 4:05.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["9:15", "/^\\s*0?9\\s*[:.]\\s*15\\s*(a\\.?m\\.?|p\\.?m\\.?)?\\s*$/i"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u08s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minute hand on 2. Minutes past?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u08s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minute hand on 12. Minutes past?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m3u08s1m05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Breakfast at 7:00 is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "a.m.", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "p.m.", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m3u08s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes in an hour?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 60, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c3u08", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 8.1 notes · Telling the time", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "8.2", "title": "Days, weeks, months and years", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Birthday countdown", "p": ["Today is **3 May**. Leo's birthday is **17 May**.", "How many days until his birthday? How many weeks is that? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Days of the week", "p": ["Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday."], "qq": {"id": "m3u08s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Days in a week?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Units of time", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Unit", "Equals"], "rows": [["1 minute", "60 seconds"], ["1 hour", "60 minutes"], ["1 day", "24 hours"], ["1 week", "7 days"], ["1 year", "12 months, 52 weeks, 365 days (366 in a leap year)"]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Using a calendar", "p": ["Count on in a calendar: 3 May → 17 May is **14 days** = **2 weeks**.", "Months have 28–31 days. '30 days has September, April, June and November'; February has 28 (29 in a leap year); the rest have 31."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Days", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u08s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Days in 3 weeks?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 21, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "21."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I use units of time and a calendar?", "p": ["Step 1: Know the conversions (7 days = 1 week…).", "Step 2: On a calendar, count on from the start date.", "Step 3: Remember how many days each month has.", "Step 4: Change days to weeks by dividing by 7."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Weeks", "p": [], "q": "28 days in weeks.", "steps": [["28 ÷ 7", ""]], "a": "4 weeks"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Next month", "p": [], "q": "28 June + 5 days.", "steps": [["June has 30 days", ""], ["29, 30, 1, 2, 3", ""]], "a": "3 July"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order", "p": [], "q": "The month after August.", "steps": [["…July, August, September", ""]], "a": "September"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Day", "p": [], "q": "If today is Tuesday, what day is it in 10 days?", "steps": [["7 days → Tuesday", ""], ["3 more → Friday", ""]], "a": "Friday"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Month", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u08s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Days in April?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 30, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "30."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Thinking every month has 30 days", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Days in January.", "lines": ["30"], "bad": 0, "why": "January has 31 days.", "fix": [["31", ""]], "id": "m3u08s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Thinking all months are the same length", "p": ["Use the rhyme or your knuckles to check."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Planning holidays, counting down to birthdays and school terms use calendars."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["60 s = 1 min; 60 min = 1 h; 24 h = 1 day; 7 days = 1 week.", "12 months = 1 year.", "Months have 28–31 days."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "8.2-k1", "t":